### Canvas Editor POC API collection (VS Code REST Client / IntelliJ HTTP Client).
### Run requests top to bottom. Responses feed the variables below with `# @name` captures.
### Local only: fake owner identity via X-Owner-Id, no real auth.

@api = http://127.0.0.1:3000
@owner = demo-owner-1
@gc = http://127.0.0.1:3104
@transcoder = http://127.0.0.1:3103

### Health
GET {{api}}/healthz

### 1. Reserve an upload. sha256 = `sha256sum fixtures/sample-5.jpg`, size = `stat -c%s fixtures/sample-5.jpg`
# @name upload
POST {{api}}/v1/uploads
X-Owner-Id: {{owner}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sha256": "<64 hex chars>", "content_type": "image/jpeg", "size_bytes": 12345, "filename": "sample-5.jpg" }

### 2. PUT the bytes to upload_url from the response, with the headers in upload_headers:
###    curl -X PUT "<upload_url>" -H "Content-Type: image/jpeg" --data-binary @fixtures/sample-5.jpg

@assetId = {{upload.response.body.asset_id}}

### 3. Tell the API the upload is done (optional: the S3 event does the same)
POST {{api}}/v1/uploads/{{assetId}}/complete
X-Owner-Id: {{owner}}

### 4. Poll until processing_status is READY (PENDING | PROCESSING | READY | FAILED | REJECTED | EXPIRED)
GET {{api}}/v1/assets/{{assetId}}
X-Owner-Id: {{owner}}

### 5. Create a draft (document optional; default is an empty canvas)
# @name draft
POST {{api}}/v1/drafts
X-Owner-Id: {{owner}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "document": { "version": 1, "canvas": { "width": 1080, "height": 1080 },
  "elements": [ { "id": "e0", "type": "media", "asset_id": "{{assetId}}", "x": 0, "y": 0, "width": 100, "height": 100 } ] } }

@draftId = {{draft.response.body.draft_id}}

### 6. Save the next revision. A stale base_revision returns 409 REVISION_CONFLICT.
PUT {{api}}/v1/drafts/{{draftId}}
X-Owner-Id: {{owner}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "base_revision": 1, "document": { "version": 1, "canvas": { "width": 1080, "height": 1080 },
  "elements": [ { "id": "e0", "type": "media", "asset_id": "{{assetId}}", "x": 10, "y": 0, "width": 100, "height": 100 } ] } }

### 7. Read, list, revisions, restore an old revision (creates a new head)
GET {{api}}/v1/drafts/{{draftId}}
X-Owner-Id: {{owner}}

###
GET {{api}}/v1/drafts
X-Owner-Id: {{owner}}

###
GET {{api}}/v1/drafts/{{draftId}}/revisions
X-Owner-Id: {{owner}}

###
POST {{api}}/v1/drafts/{{draftId}}/revisions/1/restore
X-Owner-Id: {{owner}}

### 8. Mock AI layout (202 first time, 200 cached: true afterwards)
# @name ai
POST {{api}}/v1/drafts/{{draftId}}/ai-layouts
X-Owner-Id: {{owner}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "asset_ids": ["{{assetId}}"], "seed": 7 }

###
GET {{api}}/v1/ai-layouts/{{ai.response.body.generation_id}}
X-Owner-Id: {{owner}}

### Accept the READY layout as a new AI_GENERATION revision
POST {{api}}/v1/drafts/{{draftId}}/ai-layouts/{{ai.response.body.generation_id}}/accept
X-Owner-Id: {{owner}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "base_revision": 2 }

### 9. Publish an exact revision. Idempotency-Key is required. One publication per draft.
# @name pub
POST {{api}}/v1/drafts/{{draftId}}/publications
X-Owner-Id: {{owner}}
Idempotency-Key: demo-key-1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "revision": 1 }

@pubId = {{pub.response.body.publication_id}}

### 10. Poll. status goes REQUESTED > WAITING_FOR_ASSETS > TRANSCODING > AWAITING_CANVAS
GET {{api}}/v1/publications/{{pubId}}
X-Owner-Id: {{owner}}

### 11. In AWAITING_CANVAS: get an upload URL for the rendered canvas, PUT the file, then confirm
# @name canvas
POST {{api}}/v1/publications/{{pubId}}/canvas-upload
X-Owner-Id: {{owner}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "content_type": "image/png", "size_bytes": 1234 }

### curl -X PUT "<upload_url>" -H "Content-Type: image/png" --data-binary @fixtures/canvas-render.png

###
POST {{api}}/v1/publications/{{pubId}}/canvas-uploaded
X-Owner-Id: {{owner}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "content_type": "image/png" }

### 12. After a failure: retry on the same publication (reuses READY finals)
POST {{api}}/v1/publications/{{pubId}}/retry
X-Owner-Id: {{owner}}

### Draft status roll-up (assets + publication)
GET {{api}}/v1/drafts/{{draftId}}/status
X-Owner-Id: {{owner}}

### Discard (soft) and restore a draft
DELETE {{api}}/v1/drafts/{{draftId}}
X-Owner-Id: {{owner}}

###
POST {{api}}/v1/drafts/{{draftId}}/restore
X-Owner-Id: {{owner}}

### ---- Operations (gc-worker, localhost only) ----

### Run one GC cycle, or named steps: ?step=sweep or ?step=reconcileUploads,reconcileDrift
POST {{gc}}/run

### Failed or stuck jobs, DLQ contents, move DLQ messages back to the source queue
GET {{gc}}/ops/jobs

###
GET {{gc}}/ops/dlq

###
POST {{gc}}/ops/redrive

### Mock transcoder job state for an asset: QUEUED | RUNNING | COMPLETE | ERROR
GET {{transcoder}}/jobs?asset_id={{assetId}}
